@page "/privacy"
@layout MarketingLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>@L["PrivacyPolicy"] - LearnStack</PageTitle>

<article class="privacy-policy">
    <h1>@L["PrivacyPolicy"]</h1>
    <h2>@L["Essential application data"]</h2>
    <p>@L["LearnStack stores account details and the learning resources, notes and content ideas you save to provide the service. Authentication and language cookies support sign-in and your chosen language; they are not analytics consent."]</p>
    <h2>@L["Optional analytics"]</h2>
    <p>@L["With your explicit consent, LearnStack uses Microsoft Clarity to understand page usage through cookies, heatmaps and session recordings. Clarity receives usage and interaction data, page URLs, device and browser information. It is a third-party Microsoft service, not first-party or cookieless analytics. Advertising consent is always denied."]</p>
    <p>@L["Clarity is not loaded before you accept analytics. Page text is masked for recordings; LearnStack does not send account identifiers to Clarity. Your choice is stored in this browser for up to 180 days."]</p>
    <p>@L["Use Analytics preferences on this page or in the account menu to reject analytics or withdraw consent at any time. Withdrawal removes LearnStack's Clarity cookies and reloads the page to stop tracking. It does not delete data already collected by Microsoft."]</p>
    <p><a href="/privacy?analytics=preferences">@L["Analytics preferences"]</a></p>
    <p><a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@L["Microsoft privacy statement"]</a></p>
    <p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/clarity/setup-and-installation/data-retention" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@L["Clarity data retention"]</a></p>
    <h2>@L["Your data and choices"]</h2>
    <p>@L["You can use LearnStack without accepting analytics. Account management provides personal data download and account deletion. Shared collections and resources you choose to publish are visible to their intended audience."]</p>
    <p>@L["The personal data download in account management is a JSON file containing your account details, external login keys, and everything you have saved: learning resources and notes, content ideas, shared collections, friendships and invitations, and your plan. Cached thumbnail images are not included, because they are copies of images from the original websites."]</p>
</article>
